scenario_id: dpgd-116
theme: gilligans-island
run_id: 2
total_caught: 3
total_findings: 7
weighted_caught: 15
total_weight: 37
score_pct: 40.5
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase addressed from_file_or_default swallowing all errors. The config
    tests check loading behavior but none test that parse/permission errors are distinguished
    from NotFound.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer finding #5: 'ServerError Display leaks raw server response body\
    \ (CWE-209)' \u2014 flags that Display impl passes raw HTTP body to user-visible\
    \ output. TEA also wrote security tests for CWE-209 but they used keyword allowlists\
    \ rather than real sanitization, which the reviewer called out as insufficient."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote header injection tests for tenant ID and auth token (CWE-113)\
    \ in siem_client.rs and security.rs. Dev implemented HeaderValue::from_str() which\
    \ rejects CRLF. However, the underlying issue of using raw String instead of TenantId\
    \ from axiathon-core was NOT flagged \u2014 only the injection symptom was addressed,\
    \ not the type-safety root cause."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: 'No phase flagged that dependencies use direct version strings instead
    of workspace = true. The reviewer noted a toml version mismatch (finding #8) but
    did not flag the workspace inheritance pattern violation.'
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer finding #6: 'RawConfig silently ignores unknown TOML fields'\
    \ \u2014 explicitly flags that without #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)], a config\
    \ with 'token = my-secret' is silently accepted, giving a false sense of security."
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    true). TEA wrote config tests but the specific assertion logic flaw was not caught.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: 'No phase flagged the test with zero assertions that only checks non-panic.
    Despite SOUL.md principle #4 about silent failures and vacuously true tests, this
    was missed.'
